# AGENTS.md — {{ project_name }}

Single source of instructions for AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor,
Gemini CLI, Copilot, neo-harness, …), following the [agents.md](https://agents.md)
convention. `CLAUDE.md` is a one-line `@AGENTS.md` import and
`.gemini/settings.json` points Gemini CLI here, so keep everything in this file.

## Overview

**{{ project_name }}** — {{ description }}  
**Org:** {{ org_name }}

This is a **monorepo control plane**. Prefer layout discipline, small reviewable
changes, and explicit validation. Do not treat `workspace/` as durable product
documentation.

## Session bootstrap (recommended)

1. Read [LAYOUT.md](LAYOUT.md).  
2. Read this file, then [WORKFLOW.md](WORKFLOW.md) and [BUSINESS.md](BUSINESS.md) for constraints.  
3. If shared graph/RAG (or other platform services) are configured for this lab,
   **validate them before asserting live status** (health endpoint, MCP, or
   documented probe). Do not invent “healthy” from memory.  
4. Prefer work on a feature or session branch — never commit secrets.

## Monorepo layout (read first)

```text
products/   → ship code
services/   → shared platform services
hosts/      → IaC
lab/        → experiments (never ship as-is)
docs/       → durable knowledge
workspace/  → scratch only
```

```bash
python3 scripts/print_layout.py   # print the layout registry
python3 -m pytest tests -q        # layout smoke tests (same as CI)
```

Do **not** invent top-level directories. Put durable notes in `docs/`, not
`workspace/`.

## Agent instructions

1. Change the **smallest** correct bucket (`products/`, `services/`, `hosts/`, …).  
2. For host/system changes: prefer IaC under `hosts/` over ad-hoc machine edits.  
3. Keep product vs lab boundaries clear (`products/` / `services/` vs `lab/`).  
4. Record durable decisions in `docs/decisions/`.  
5. If neo-harness is embedded, prefer `./scripts/neo` for bounded jobs.

## Stack

- Python {{ python_version }}+ for monorepo tooling and packages  
- Prefer package managers and language stacks declared in `BUSINESS.md`  
- Nested product trees may use their own tooling (and their own `AGENTS.md`)

## Git workflow

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `main` | Production-ready / releases |
| `{{ default_integration_branch }}` | Integration (daily work) |
| `feat/*`, `fix/*`, `docs/*`, `chore/*` | Short-lived local work |

- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, …  
- Branch off the integration branch; merge back with review (`--squash` for one
  clean commit), then delete the branch  
- Never commit `.env` or credentials  

## Coding standards

- Type hints on public Python APIs  
- Tests for non-trivial behavior  
- Document durable decisions under `docs/decisions/`  

## neo-harness (if embedded)

Constrained PLAN→ACT→REFLECT jobs use the workspace runner (not a global
`neo` assumed on PATH):

```bash
./scripts/neo doctor
./scripts/neo start --task-file jobs/<slug>.md --agent workspace -p mock
```

- Install/refresh: project `.venv-neo` + `requirements-neo.txt` (or editable neo-harness)  
- Docs: [starting-a-workspace](https://github.com/westailabs/neo-harness/blob/master/docs/starting-a-workspace.md)  
- Upstream: https://github.com/westailabs/neo-harness  

## Shared services (generic stub)

If this monorepo documents shared retrieval or knowledge-graph services:

| Rule | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| Before asserting status | Probe health / live query |
| If unreachable | Say so; continue only with local offline work |
| Secrets | Env / secret store only — never commit tokens |

Concrete URLs and tokens are **environment-specific** — see operator docs under
`docs/ops/` when filled in.

## Hard rules

- No secrets in git (`.env`, keys, vault material)  
- IaC for hosts lives under `hosts/` — prefer declared state over one-off shell  
- Product code in `products/` or `services/`, not `lab/` until promoted  
- Prefer tests for behavior changes at monorepo or package level  
